# Numbering

The plans are in :ref[tbl:plans], the prices in :ref[tbl:prices], and :ref[tbl:plans, tbl:prices] together. :ref[eq:energy] and :ref[eq:mass, eq:energy] come later on the page, and so does :ref[sec:the-equations].

## The tables

:::table[What each plan costs](id=tbl:plans)
| plan | price |
| --- | --- |
| free | 0 |
| pro | 10 |
:::

:::table[Prices by year](id=tbl:prices)
| year | price |
| --- | --- |
| 2025 | 9 |
| 2026 | 10 |
:::

A table with no id has a caption and no number:

:::table[Not numbered]
| a |
| --- |
| 1 |
:::

## The equations

```math id=eq:energy
E = mc^2
```

```math id=eq:mass
m = \frac{E}{c^2}
```

A math fence with no id is not numbered:

```math
a^2 + b^2 = c^2
```

As :ref[eq:energy] shows, :ref[tbl:plans] is cheap. A reference to nothing reads :ref[fig:missing], and is a warning in the terminal of the dev server.
